  "description": "A museum's own collection as K-samsök (Riksantikvarieämbetet) publishes it, live: a map of find places and places, a time line of dating, object names and materials, pictures with their licence and a link to each record, and the collection gaps (the share of records without coordinates, dating, a picture or a licence, by record type and object name) that public-access reporting asks about. Set the org parameter to another institution's K-samsök code (shm, nomu, jlm, upmu, ...) and the parish parameter to look wider: that parish's ancient monuments in Fornsök and every institution with records from it. Statistics: the gaps, dating, names and materials are counted by K-samsök over the whole set (facets), so they are exact, not sampled; a record dated over a range counts in every century it spans. The map and the pictures are one page each (150 and 36 records, in K-samsök's order: not a random sample), and the board says how many there are in all. Caveats: K-samsök shows what the museum last delivered to it, which can lag its own system; a museum that keeps photographs as separate media records (SHM does) shows its objects without a picture here; a facet lists only its 100 largest terms, so small object names' gaps are upper bounds. Built to embed on the museum's own site and to run as a kiosk in the gallery.",
